senses.gloss:
प्र-दत्त, अस्, आ, अम्, given away, given, offered,
presented, bestowed, granted; given in marriage;
(अस्), m., N. of a Gandharva.

प्र-दातव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be given away, to be
given; to be given back; to be given in marriage;
to be placed in or put into.

प्र-दर्शन, अम्, n. foreshowing, prophesying;
look, appearance, aspect, (often at the end of comps.,
e. g. घोर-प्˚, of terrible aspect); showing, pointing
out, manifesting, displaying, bringing to light, indi-
cating; explaining, specifying, teaching; an example;
(आस्), m. pl. a class of deities under Manu Auttami.

प्रादेशिन्, ई, इनी, इ (fr. प्रादेश), a span long;
(इनी), f. the forefinger, (in this sense probably an
error for प्र-देशिनी.)
